# Component Conventions

## File Naming
1. Use kebab-case for all component files
```typescript
// ✅ Good
connected-accounts.tsx
all-posts.tsx
user-profile.tsx

// ❌ Bad
ConnectedAccounts.tsx
AllPosts.tsx
userProfile.tsx
```

## Component Imports
1. Import UI components from `@delulu/design-system/components/ui/*`
```typescript
// ✅ Good
import { Button } from "@delulu/design-system/components/ui/button";
import { Input } from "@delulu/design-system/components/ui/input";
import { Card } from "@delulu/design-system/components/ui/card";

// ❌ Bad
import { Button } from "@delulu/ui/button";
import { Input } from "../components/ui/input";
```

2. Import utility functions from `@delulu/design-system/lib`
```typescript
// ✅ Good
import { cn } from "@delulu/design-system/lib/utils";

// ❌ Bad
import { cn } from "~/lib/utils";
import { cn } from "@delulu/ui/utils";
```

## Component Declaration
1. Use function declarations instead of arrow functions
```typescript
// ✅ Good
export default function ConnectedAccounts() {
  return (
    // JSX
  );
}

// ✅ Good for sub-components
export function AccountCard({ account }: AccountCardProps) {
  return (
    // JSX
  );
}

// ❌ Bad
const ConnectedAccounts: React.FC<Props> = () => {
  return (
    // JSX
  );
};
```

2. Export main page components as default, sub-components as named exports
```typescript
// ✅ Good - Main page component
export default function ConnectedAccounts() {
  // Implementation
}

// ✅ Good - Sub-component
export function AccountCard() {
  // Implementation
}

// ❌ Bad
export const ConnectedAccounts = () => {
  // Implementation
};
```

## Component Organization
1. Group related components in a directory
```
components/
├── connected-accounts/
│   ├── connected-accounts.tsx
│   ├── account-card.tsx
│   ├── account-filters.tsx
│   └── account-stats.tsx
└── posts/
    ├── all-posts.tsx
    ├── post-card.tsx
    └── post-filters.tsx
```

2. Keep component-specific types and utilities close to the component
```typescript
// In connected-accounts.tsx or types.ts in the same directory
interface AccountCardProps {
  account: SocialProvider;
  onConnect: (platform: SocialType) => void;
}
```
